    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive strategy today hinges on capitalizing on favorable velocity profiles and wind conditions, with **Andy Pages** (70.07) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) leading the charge as our premier starts. **Andy Pages** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Kochanowicz, whose 5.12 xERA offers the most favorable ceiling in the current rotation. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s matchup against Painter is significantly boosted by environmental factors; a 0.379 xwOBA combined with a strong wind-out projection and a leadoff spot makes him a high-efficiency engine for Runs and OBP. While **Gunnar Henderson** (63.31) faces a stiffer test against Fisher, his elite ability to exploit the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery tempo provides a critical edge for our stolen base-heavy mandate, mitigating the risk of a sub-3.20 xERA opponent.\n\nOur most difficult selection decision today involved **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 41.36. While **Brayan Rocchio** offers utility value, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Miguel Vargas** (61.96) in the UTIL slot, whose exposure to the same favorable wind conditions and higher lineup placement outweighed **Brayan Rocchio**\u2019s lower-order constraints. We are closely monitoring the bottom of the lineup, as **Dominic Smith** (42.40) sits just above our sub-40 floor; he is a strict \"start-only\" necessity today due to his platoon edge against Ashcraft, but he remains the first candidate for pinch-hit substitution should the game script turn sour. \n\nWe maintain a conservative outlook on our core sluggers facing high-tier pitching; **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.19), **Josh Jung** (53.90), and **Jackson Merrill** (53.80) are all being deployed in \"marginal\" territory. **Jackson Merrill**, in particular, faces a significant drag from the opposing catcher\u2019s elite 1.87s pop time, which directly conflicts with our focus on SB efficiency. As always, we are continuing to manage the recovery of **Jordan Westburg** on the IL and will re-evaluate our infield depth once he moves closer to a rehab assignment. With the current lineup, the objective remains steady: prioritize high-floor speed production from **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** while waiting for the middle-order anchors to capitalize on any mistakes from the opposing arms.",
